    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-aranya-kanda-0045",
      "sequence": 751,
      "meaning": "Hearing Rāma's lovely words, the sage's body thrilled and his eyes filled with tears. He exclaimed, ‘What other Lord has such a way—such possessive affection and love for a servant? Those poor in knowledge, dull and unfortunate, who do not worship such a Lord after abandoning delusion!’ Nārada then spoke respectfully: ‘Hear me, Rāma, master of realization. Tell me the characteristics of saints, hero of Raghu, Lord who destroys the fear of becoming.’ Rāma replied, ‘Hear, sage, as I tell the saints' virtues, through which I remain under their loving influence. They have conquered the six passions, are sinless, desireless, unwavering, possessionless, pure and abodes of happiness. Their understanding is boundless; they are without craving, moderate in enjoyment, rooted in truth, inspired poets, learned and united in yoga. They are vigilant, give honour, lack pride, are steadfast, and are supremely accomplished in the path of dharma. Treasuries of virtue, free from worldly suffering and devoid of doubt, they abandon attachment to my lotus feet neither for body nor home; nothing is dearer to them.’",
