      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-aranya-kanda-0046",
      "sequence": 752,
      "meaning": "‘Saints feel shy when hearing their own virtues and rejoice still more when hearing another's. Equanimous and cool-tempered, they never abandon right conduct; their nature is straightforward and they love everyone. They practise recitation, austerity, vows, self-restraint, control, and disciplines, and love the feet of teacher, Govinda and Brahmins. They possess faith, forgiveness, friendship, compassion, sympathetic joy and guileless love for my feet. They have detachment, discernment, humility, realization and true understanding of the Vedas and Purāṇas. They show no hypocrisy, self-importance or pride toward anyone and never mistakenly set foot upon an evil path. They always sing and hear my divine play, are dedicated without ulterior motive to others' welfare, and are virtuous. Hear, sage: neither Śāradā nor all the Vedas can express the saints' innumerable virtues.’",
